Subject: [PATCH 101/119] docs: Sensor Clip, the writer clamp, and a third
 round of tests

README gains the Sensor Clip property with the sentence that matters - the
clip is after the white balance, which is why a blown highlight stays white -
and the note that the lens effects upstream are deliberately not clipped.

ConsoleReference gains r_SceneReferredWriterClamp: what it bounds, why it is a
format bound and not a look, why the sky's Mie peak and a night-exposed
emissive are the two writers that need it, why 2^15 and not 2^16, and that
setting it to 0 is how to see the overflow it prevents.

TEST-CHECKLIST (in scene-notes, not tracked here) gains a third round in the
same shape as the second: causes first in plain language, then sun-in-frame,
white balance and Sensor Clip 10/14/18, the night lamp's FFT rays at Streak
Amount 50, and a regression pass that asks specifically whether the moved
firefly knee left any sparkle flickering.

