+++ b/Code/CryPlugins/CinematicCamera/README.md
@@ -224,6 +224,7 @@ other than the neutral exposure.
 | Auto Exposure Response Time | 0-10 s (slider 0-5) | 1.0 | **Scene Referred only.** Seconds for the metered EV to cover 63 % of a change. A camera cut always snaps instantly. 0 = no smoothing. |
 | Auto Exposure EV Min | -6 to 24 | -2.0 | **Scene Referred only.** The brightest the camera will open up to (low EV = open). |
 | Auto Exposure EV Max | -6 to 24 | 20.0 | **Scene Referred only.** The darkest the camera will stop down to (high EV = closed). |
+| Sensor Clip (stops over grey) | 8-20 | 14.0 | **Scene Referred only.** The sensor's full well. Highlights are clipped per channel at this many stops above mid grey, **after** the white balance, so a clipped highlight stays white at every colour temperature instead of taking the balance's tint - which is what every RAW converter does and why a blown sky in a real camera is white and not blue. 14 matches the exposure meter's own ceiling. Lower = a smaller, earlier-clipping sensor (more flat white sky); higher = highlight colour and structure a long way up. The lens effects upstream - bloom, glare, diffraction, depth of field - are deliberately **not** clipped: the lens sees the real light, so a sun a hundred thousand times over the clip still throws a flare that says so. |
 
 ### Depth Of Field
 
